DevOps is a set of practices, tools, and cultural philosophies that combine software development
(Dev) and IT operations (Ops) to build, test, and release software faster and more reliably.
The DevOps Lifecycle StagesPlan & Code: Teams outline project goals and manage source code using version control systems like GitLab.Build
Test: Code is automatically compiled and checked for bugs or security flaws through automated testing.
Deploy: Applications are rolled out to production using platforms like Kubernetes or automated CI/CD pipelines.Operate 
Monitor: Systems track performance metrics and logs to ensure high availability and user satisfaction.
